---
import {site} from '../../config/site.mjs';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
export function getStaticPaths(){return site.template === 'client' ? [] : [{params:{index:undefined}}];}
const page={slug:'audits',title:'AI-app security reviews — Coming soon | EZERWRIGHT',description:'Explore the planned EZERWRIGHT source-code security review service for AI-built apps. Written authorization, defined scope and evidence-based reporting. Coming soon.'};
---
<Layout page={page}>
<section class="atelier-audit-hero" aria-labelledby="audit-title"><div class="audit-hero-rings" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="container"><span class="atelier-badge">COMING SOON / IN PREPARATION</span><h1 id="audit-title">You built the idea.<br/><em>Look a little deeper.</em></h1><p class="atelier-lead">An app can look finished before everything underneath has been examined. We’re preparing a source-code security review service for AI-built and vibe-coded applications.</p><div class="atelier-actions"><a class="atelier-button" href="/contact/?service=other">Ask about future availability <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="atelier-text-link" href="#audit-direction">Explore the planned review ↓</a></div></div></section>
<section class="container atelier-audit-content" id="audit-direction" aria-labelledby="audit-direction-title"><p class="atelier-kicker">A PLANNED SERVICE, NOT AN AUTOMATED SECURITY BADGE</p><h2 id="audit-direction-title">Evidence before reassurance.</h2><p>We are validating the tools, reporting process and delivery model before taking audit bookings. Pricing, turnaround and final scope are not yet published. An enquiry expresses interest; it does not commission or authorize a security test.</p><div class="atelier-audit-grid"><article data-reveal><span>01 / DEFINE</span><h3>The right access.<br/>The right boundaries.</h3><p>A proposed review starts with written authorization, a defined application version, source-code access and agreed exclusions. A public website address alone is not enough for a full source review.</p></article><article data-reveal><span>02 / EXAMINE</span><h3>Beyond the<br/>polished interface.</h3><p>The proposed scope considers authentication, authorization, data boundaries, sensitive-data handling and other relevant code paths. What is examined depends on the application and the agreed scope.</p></article><article data-reveal><span>03 / EXPLAIN</span><h3>Clear evidence.<br/>Useful next steps.</h3><p>The intended report separates supported findings, areas needing further validation and untested areas, with source references and practical remediation guidance. No invented vulnerabilities or inflated certainty.</p></article></div><div class="atelier-audit-boundary" data-reveal><h2>Clarity about what this is—and isn’t.</h2><p>This is not a certification or a guarantee that an application is secure. AI-generated code is not automatically vulnerable, and a clean review cannot establish that no vulnerabilities exist.</p><p>The service is being developed around an AI-assisted, source-first review workflow, including evaluation of Cloudflare’s open-source security-audit-skill. EZERWRIGHT is independent; no Cloudflare affiliation, endorsement or certification is implied.</p><p>Live penetration testing, production exploitation, compliance certification, implementation of fixes and deployment are outside this proposed service unless separately scoped and explicitly authorized. Do not send passwords, secret keys, private code or customer data through the enquiry form.</p><a class="atelier-text-link" href="/contact/?service=other">Discuss your requirements by email ↗</a></div></section>
</Layout>
